@startuml
' Source of truth for: assets/diagrams/learning/data-plane/ngfw/startup-sequence.svg
' Re-render with: plantuml -tsvg startup-sequence.puml
title Startup Sequence\n(orchestrator brings the planes up in dependency order)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

start
:1. Render config from templates\n(envsubst fills env-file values into startup + interface config);
:2. Launch VPP (data plane)\nbinds NICs via DPDK, starts worker threads on pinned cores;
:3. Apply interface config\nVLAN sub-ifaces, IPs, feature arcs, NAT enable — the pipeline;
:4. Start Snort IPS instances\nN processes pinned to cores; each attaches to VPP via the DAQ;
:5. Start IKE daemon (control)\nStrongSwan charon, ready to negotiate VPN tunnels;
:6. Start management bridge\nJava process attaches to VPP stats/API; serves counters northbound;
:7. Seed management ACL rules\nbaseline permit rules so the box is reachable for management;
stop

note right
Data plane first, then the engines
that plug into it, then control,
then management.
end note
@enduml
